nitor and diagnose a social network application composed of many microservices. Some might have faults, and I need to find the root cause. \n\nFirst, I need to figure out what services are running in the cluster. The user mentioned using the get_services tool, which retrieves service names from Grafana. That makes sense because Grafana often displays monitoring data, including services. So, I'll call get_services to get the list of services.\n\nWait, the tool's description says it returns a list of service names available in Grafana. But does Grafana directly list Kubernetes services, or is it more about dashboards and metrics? Maybe the services here refer to the application's services, not the Kubernetes ones. But regardless, starting with get_services is logical to get the initial list.\n\nOnce I have the services, I can then check each one for issues. But first, let's get the list. So the tool call should be straightforward. No arguments needed for get_services. Just invoke it and proceed with the results.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'get_services'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8974a1437f22f523', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 236, 'prompt_tokens': 2463, 'total_tokens': 2699, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfda0-dcd2-7e33-9d1e-d4975def2ba1-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_services', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8974a1437f22f523', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2463, 'output_tokens': 236, 'total_tokens': 2699}), ToolMessage(content="meta=None content=[TextContent(type='text', text='None', annotations=None)] isError=False", id='82e41020-b31d-4ca4-b20e-685b9661da9d', tool_call_id='c