     volumes:\n      - configMap:\n          defaultMode: 420\n          name: media-service\n        name: media-service-config\nstatus:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T21:08:17Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T21:08:17Z"\n    message: Deployment does not have minimum availability.\n    reason: MinimumReplicasUnavailable\n    status: "False"\n    type: Available\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T21:08:17Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T21:08:17Z"\n    message: ReplicaSet "media-service-554cbbf9cb" is progressing.\n    reason: ReplicaSetUpdated\n    status: "True"\n    type: Progressing\n  observedGeneration: 1\n  replicas: 1\n  unavailableReplicas: 1\n  updatedReplicas: 1\n', id='46185963-487a-4f43-8739-fcb2e4c33802', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-912697f40cfe866a'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='72e89984-251e-43fd-8809-b9dd41499293'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The media-service pod is pending because of a port conflict. The deployment specifies hostPort: 9100, and all nodes have that port occupied. So the solution is to change the hostPort to an unused port. But first, I need to check which ports are currently in use across the cluster to pick an available one. \n\nWait, but maybe I can just pick a different port, like 9101, and update the deployment. However, I should confirm that the new port isn\'t already taken. But since the error message says all nodes have port 9100 occupied, maybe 9101 is free. Alternatively, maybe I should check the current port usage to be safe. \n\nBut the user might not have a tool to check port usage directly. The available tools are get_traces, get_services, get_operations, get_dependency_graph, get_metrics, exec_kubectl_cmd_safely, wait_tool, and submit_tool. \n\nHmm, maybe I can use exec_kubectl_cmd_safely to check the node ports. For example, run `kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath=\'{.items[*].status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}\'` to get node IPs, then check each node\'s port usage. But that\'s complicated. Alternatively, maybe the user can just update the hostPort to 9101 and see if that works. \n\nSince the error is about no free ports for 9100, changing it to 9101 might resolve the issue. So the next step is to update the deployment\'s hostPort to 9101. Let me use exec_kubectl_cmd_safely to edit the deployment. But wait, the user can\'t use interactive commands like kubectl edit. So I need to generate a YAML patch to update the hostPort. \n\nThe command would be to apply a patch to the deployment. So the correct tool is exec_kubectl_cmd_safely with the command to apply the patch. Let me construct that command.\n</think>\n\nexec_kubectl_cmd_safely\nTo resolve the "no free ports" error, we need to update the **hostPort** in the media-service deployment from `9100` to an unused port (e.g., `9101`). This will allow the pod to schedule on a node with an available port. The command will modify the deployment\'s pod spec to use the new port. \n\nThe command to update the deployment is:  \n`kubectl patch deployment media-service -n social-network -p \'{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"media-service","ports":[{"containerPort":9090,"hostPort":9101,"protocol":"TCP"}]}]}}}}\'`', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 581, 'prompt_tokens': 5699, 'total_tokens': 6280, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfda1-f445-70a2-8772-38334ce778fa-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5699, 'output_tokens': 581, 'total_tokens': 6280}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0db28805-62d6-4afe-9c66-b08e0400e572'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to fix the media-service pod that's in a Pending state because of a port conflict. The previous steps showed that the pod's hostPort is set to 9100, which is already occupied on all nodes. The solution was to change the hostPort to 9101. \n\nNow, the user has chosen the exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool again. The command they provided is a kubectl patch to update the deployment's hostPort. I need to verify if this command is correct.\n\nThe command uses the patch method to update the deployment. The JSON specifies changing the hostPort to 9101 for the media-service container. This should resolve the port conflict. However, I should check if the syntax is correct. The patch command structure looks right, targeting the correct deployment and updating the template's spec. \n\nWait, the original deployment's hostPort was 9100. The patch replaces that with 9101. That makes sense. After applying this change, the pod should be able to schedule because the port is now available. \n\nI should also consider if there are any other issues. For example, if another service is using 9101, but the error message indicated that 9100 was the problem. Assuming 9101 is free, this should work. \n\nSo, the tool call is correct. The next step is to execute this command and then check if the pod status changes. If it does, the issue is resolved. If not, further investigation might be needed, but the user's plan is to proceed with this fix.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl patch deployment media-service -n social-network -p \'{\\"spec\\":{\\"template\\":{\\"spec\\":{\\"containers\\":[{\\"name\\":\\"media-service\\",\\"ports\\":[{\\"containerPort\\":9090,\\"hostPort\\":9101,\\"protocol\\":\\"TCP\\"}]}]}}}}\'"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b341ef00f672aa8b', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 427, 'prompt_tokens': 6871, 'total_tokens': 7298, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfda2-1048-7530-8b18-45e471dde718-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl patch deployment media-service -n social-network -p \'{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"media-service","ports":[{"containerPort":9090,"hostPort":9101,"protocol":"TCP"}]}]}}}}\''}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b341ef00f672aa8b', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6871, 'output_tokens': 427, 'total_tokens': 7298}), ToolMessage(content='deployment.apps/media-service patched\n', id='47f80797-d950-4060-9663-e86c4aa8d73d', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-b341ef00f672aa8b'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='dadc2450-7435-4ef5-9754-327e4b25fe2e')]]
